  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 1208 AM CST Sat Nov 14 2026\n\nSunday night winds will switch to northeasterly pushing the showers \nout of the area and bringing cooler, drier air. An upper level ridge \nwill move in starting Monday bringing dry weather back that will \ncontinue through the day Wednesday. Moisture will surge from the \nGulf bringing low chances for rain Thursday and Friday.\n\nMonday the northeasterly winds will bring the cooler, drier air. \nModels are showing cooler temperatures for Monday and Tuesday and \nthey have continued to trend lower the last few days. Monday highs \nwill not reach 60 everywhere except the southern Rio Grande Plains. \nThe low level flow will become easterly to southeasterly starting \nWednesday and warmer air will return for the rest of the period.",
